OL,3,GNEWSAAutistic student defies odds to
OL,4,Apass his GCSEs
OL,5,
OL,6,FFrom being suspended from primary
OL,7,Fschool for his behaviour and being told
OL,8,Fhe would not be able to take his GCSEs,
OL,9,FSully has defied all odds.
OL,11,FThe teenager from Plymouth, Devon, is
OL,12,Fautistic and said he did "way better"
OL,13,Fthan he expected after opening his
OL,14,Fresults.
OL,16,FThe Tor Bridge High student said he was
OL,17,Fexpecting to get 4s in all his subjects
OL,18,Fbut received 4s,5s and even a 6 in
OL,19,FEnglish Language.
OL,21,FHis mum, Harriet, said she was
OL,22,F"eternally grateful" to the school.
